  partName: Heat Shield (2)
  description: The Heat Shield (2) is a medium-sized, thin-flat metal component situated
    at the middle-center-center of the engine, designed to protect surrounding components
    from excessive heat generated by the engine's core. Its bright metal finish suggests
    a high-temperature resistant material, which is essential for maintaining the
    shield's structural integrity. Interestingly, the heat shield's design allows
    for minimal airflow obstruction while providing effective thermal protection.
